From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 11:52:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 248/248] 3070 (a): the turn that approved the plan runs
 without ask_contact
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Misho's yes, 13 Oct 11:2x UTC in the operations chat („ჩემგან ყველაფერზე
კია", relayed verbatim by ops at 11:28Z), to the 3070 server-order changes.
The tester's 56299, trio 1: in the approval turn the model called ask_contact
twice and was refused twice („day one is already starting"). The refusals
cost the turn a second model round, and day one could not begin until 37.6 s
had passed. A turn that approved the plan (runApprovedAPlan, set by the tap
or the tool) is no longer given ask_contact at all.

Part (b), starting day one at the tap instead of after the approval reply,
is not in this commit. It would put two runs in one conversation at once,
which the one-run-per-thread rule exists to prevent. It needs its own design.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
